From ce7c9ec11a56273e04d13fd3d4385905cc6b1bf2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joeri Van Dooren <ure@on6ure.be>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] audio, ptt: the X6100/X6200 radio's own software as the sound
 card and PTT (OpenX6X00)

On the radios, OpenX6X00's GUI owns the audio and the keying: ardopcf and
Mercury reach them through its Winlink modem socket, and XARA now does
too. --audio x6x00 with --capture and --playback both the socket
(/run/ardop.sock) and --ptt x6x00, behind a cargo feature of the same
name.

audio/x6x00.rs: a thread connects, and again every second while the GUI
is not there, and says hello in the socket's protocol 2 (12000 Hz, keys
of 30 s at most, XARA's own watchdog). The receiver comes in 20 ms R
messages, up to 48 kHz with XARA's resampler; read() is paced by it and
returns zeros at the wall clock's pace while the radio transmits (no R
then) or the GUI is away. write() takes the audio down to 12 kHz and
sends it as T only between a P 1 and its P 0, which the PTT sends under
the same lock, so a transmission is exactly what the GUI was asked to
key; what the pump writes in the moment before the PTT thread keys is
held and sent right after the P 1. P 0 makes the GUI play out every T it
has, then unkey. path() gives the capture (the GUI's 20 ms fragments and
the resamplers), the key (the GUI's checks and the base) and the GUI's
playback stream as constants, 25, 50 and 80 ms until they are measured on
the radios; --x6x00-path-ms CAPTURE,KEYING,OUT sets them. No rate
matching: queue false.

main.rs checks the options together as for trusdx (one socket for both,
--ptt x6x00 with --audio x6x00 and the other way round, no
--tx-buffer-ms) and gives the PTT from the backend. With unit tests on a
fake GUI (the hello, R paced and resampled, zeros while keyed and without
the GUI, T only between P 1 and P 0, the held first block, a GUI that
goes and comes back, one that closes at once tried once a second, the
stop's P 0) and main.rs's own. One upstream test assumed the default
backend is built, which in a build with x6x00 alone it is not.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
